dish.description:
Manoomin (wild rice) cooked in ham hock stock with foraged morels and cultivated
        mushrooms, finished with spring ramps. Excavation: wild rice is Great Lakes Indigenous staple;
        ham hock stock from Southern cooking; mushroom foraging shared tradition; ramps are Appalachian.

Oxtail braised until falling-apart tender with hominy, tomatoes, and aromatics, served
        with hot pepper vinegar and skillet cornbread. Excavation: oxtail utilization from offal traditions;
        hominy is Southern and Indigenous; this is a working-class stew elevated through time and technique.

Spiced sweet potato pudding with bourbon-spiked cream and pecan brittle. Excavation:
        sweet potato puddings documented in Black cookbooks back to 1800s; bourbon Kentucky tradition;
        pecans Lower Mississippi.
